# From Small to Big — configuration.
#
# Copy to `.env` in the project root. It is auto-loaded; you do not need to
# `source` it. Real environment variables override anything set here.
#
#   cp examples/config/smalltobig.env.example .env
#
# `.env` is gitignored. Keep API keys out of the repo.

# ─────────────────────────────── web ───────────────────────────────
STB_PORT=3041
STB_HOST=127.0.0.1

# ─────────────────────────── local models ──────────────────────────
# Started separately, not supervised by this app:
#   mlx_lm.server --model <model> --port 3140
#
# Port 3140 rather than mlx_lm.server's default 8000, which collides with
# roughly every other development server. See docs/DECISIONS.md #2.
STB_LLM_BASE_URL=http://127.0.0.1:3140/v1
STB_LLM_MODEL=mlx-community/Qwen3-8B-4bit
STB_EMBED_MODEL=nomic-ai/nomic-embed-text-v2-moe

# ─────────────────────────── backend routing ───────────────────────
# Default for every stage. Leave as `local` unless you have a reason.
STB_LLM_BACKEND=local

# Per-stage overrides. Stages:
#
#   extract     chunks of ingested sources          published authors' words
#   synthesize  claim paraphrases, rule drafting    published authors' words
#   conflicts   rule imperatives                    published authors' words
#   drill       your written practice answers       yours
#   roleplay    your turns in a simulation          yours
#   judge       a roleplay transcript               yours
#   prebrief    who you are about to meet           yours AND theirs
#   debrief     what happened, and who said what    yours AND theirs
#
# `synthesize` is the stage where a larger model actually earns its cost — it
# is the hardest reasoning in the project (docs/DECISIONS.md #11) and it reads
# published books rather than anything about you. It is the usual reason to
# reach for the cloud at all.
#
# STB_LLM_BACKEND_SYNTHESIZE=openai
# STB_LLM_BACKEND_SYNTHESIZE_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# STB_LLM_BACKEND_SYNTHESIZE_MODEL=gpt-5
# STB_LLM_BACKEND_SYNTHESIZE_API_KEY=sk-...

# ─────────────────────── the field-note guard ──────────────────────
# `prebrief` and `debrief` will not use a cloud backend without this, even if
# STB_LLM_BACKEND points at one. Without it they run locally and say so.
#
# They are guarded separately because they are the only stages containing the
# words of people who are not users of this app. Someone told you something at
# an offsite. They did not agree to have it sent to a third-party API, and they
# cannot be asked now.
#
# Setting a cloud backend to debug synthesis quality is reasonable. It should
# not, as a side effect, start shipping other people's confidences offsite.
#
# STB_SEND_FIELD_NOTES_TO_CLOUD=i-understand
